haikuwebkit 1.10.0: <video> on a YCbCr overlay plane (docs/design/webpositive-video-overlay.md, WP1)

With a display that has B_YUV420 overlays, MediaPlayerPrivateHaiku decodes B_YUV420 and shows each picture on an
overlay plane of the page's BWebView (SetViewOverlay with the stream's YCbCr encoding) instead of converting it to
RGB and repainting the page: paint() fills the video's rectangle with the overlay key. Software (the player's own
YCbCr->RGB conversion) while the plane cannot be used: the video moved or is partly outside the view, content over
it changed in the last 1.5 s (the media controls), a scroll (BWebPage::scroll calls the player), no free plane, a
mode change, another video of the page has the view's plane (one overlay per BView). WEBKIT_VIDEO_OVERLAY=0 turns it off, WEBKIT_VIDEO_OVERLAY_LOG=1 prints counters.
Also: seekToTarget() returns its promise (it fell off the end); at the application's quit
(BWebPage::ShutdownOnce(), and this library's destructors) every player stops decoding and closes its file
before the decoder add-ons are unloaded (KNOWN-ISSUES F11: WebPositive crashed at quit during playback).

