+// The video on a YCbCr overlay plane
+//
+// With a display that has B_YUV420 overlays (the Raspberry Pi 4's), the
+// decoder is asked for planar B_YUV420 pictures. paint() fills the video's
+// rectangle with the overlay's colour key instead of drawing the picture, and
+// the video thread puts each new picture on an overlay plane of the page's
+// BWebView (BView::SetViewOverlay()) without repainting the page: no YCbCr to
+// RGB conversion, and none of app_server's copies of the picture. The page
+// covers the plane wherever it draws anything but the key over the video.
+// The picture is drawn in software instead (converted here) while
+// - the video's place is not known yet, or changed: the plane is moved there
+//   first, then the key is painted (key pixels written before the plane is
+//   there would stay opaque);
+// - the video is not wholly inside the view, the view is rotated or sheared,
+//   or the paint does not go to the page itself (a canvas, a snapshot);
+// - the page painted something else over the video in the last 1.5 s (the
+//   media controls: translucent pixels would blend with the key colour, not
+//   with the picture), or was scrolled in the last 0.5 s (the blit moves the
+//   key, not the plane);
+// - no plane can be had (all in use, overlays suspended for a mode change).
+// WEBKIT_VIDEO_OVERLAY=0 turns it off (B_RGB32 pictures, as before);
+// WEBKIT_VIDEO_OVERLAY_LOG=1 prints counters on stderr every 2 s.
